# Passes backendcheck.sh leaves out by default: the Metal saver draws them
# differently from GL on purpose (ss-ss8), and parity/goldencheck.sh judges them
# against approved images instead. One per line: the pass, then why and where.
# A pass goes in here in the pull request that changes its look.
stars    ss-ss8.2: no streak along a wrap (GL streaks a wrapping star for a frame); ss-ss8.3: 4x MSAA
tunnel   ss-ss8.2: true cos and sin (GL's rsCosf tables lose the argument past ~400); ss-ss8.3: 4x MSAA
sun      the stars pass with the sun in view: its stars, as stars
